# Architecture rules

Binding rules for where code lives and which direction dependencies may point.
Structure reference: [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md).

## Backend — `{{kebabCase project.name}}-backend`

Package root: `src/main/java/{{packagePath project.packageName}}`

| Layer | Package | May depend on |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Web | `controller`, `web.dto`, `web.mapper` | `service`, domain |
| Application | `service` | `repository`, domain |
| Persistence | `repository` | domain |
| Domain | `domain` | nothing (plain Java + JPA annotations) |
| Infrastructure | `config`, `security`, `exception` | any layer, but nothing may import them except the web layer |

Rules:

1. Controllers validate request DTOs and map responses; they contain no
   business logic.
2. DTO conversions happen only in `web.mapper`; DTOs never reach `service` or
   `repository` signatures.
3. Services implement use cases; one service per entity plus cross-entity use
   cases as needed. Transactions belong here.
4. Repositories are Spring Data interfaces; queries beyond derived names go in
   `@Query` methods, never in services.
5. Entities in `domain` carry JPA annotations but no HTTP or DTO types.
6. Schema changes are generated migrations
   {{#if (eq project.options.migrationTool "liquibase")}}under `src/main/resources/db/changelog/changes`{{else}}under `src/main/resources/db/migration`{{/if}},
   never manual edits to an existing migration.
7. New custom logic (extra endpoints, business rules) goes into
   `cleanstack:user-code` regions of generated files or into new classes you
   create following the naming contract.

## {{#if project.options.frontend}}Frontend — `{{kebabCase project.name}}-ui`{{else}}Frontend{{/if}}

{{#if project.options.frontend}}
Root: `src/app`

| Layer | Folder | May depend on |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Pages | `pages/<route>/{list,detail,form}` | services, models, shared |
| Services | `services` | models |
| Models | `models` | nothing |
| Shared | `shared`, `directives`, `guards`, `interceptors` | models |
| Generated client | `api/generated` | never hand-edit |

Rules:

1. One folder per route under `pages`; page components use standalone
   components and signals, not NgModules.
2. Components talk to the backend only through `services/<entity>.service.ts`;
   no `HttpClient` usage in components.
3. Types come from `models/`; do not redeclare API shapes inline.
4. Routing changes for entities are injected by the generator into
   `app.routes.ts` and `app-layout`; extend them only in protected regions.
5. `api/generated` is owned by the OpenAPI generator; never edit it.
{{else}}
This workspace was generated without a frontend. Backend rules above apply.
{{/if}}

